---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Docs — Genable" description="How Genable plans, uses typed Figma tools, keeps session context, and routes models across the plugin and MCP surfaces.">
  <section>
    <div class="container" style="max-width: 880px;">
      <span class="eyebrow">DOCS</span>
      <h1 style="margin-top: 16px;">How it works.</h1>
      <p class="lead muted" style="margin-top: 24px;">
        Genable is an agent loop over native Figma operations. It can plan from a detailed brief, call typed tools, inspect the result, and continue refining the same design. This page explains the parts that affect how you use it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section style="border-top: 1px solid var(--hair-soft);">
    <div class="container" style="max-width: 880px;">
      <h2>The agent loop</h2>
      <p class="lead muted" style="margin-top: 16px;">
        Each user turn is one <code>run()</code>. The model proposes tool calls; the tool dispatcher executes them against Figma; results return to the model; it decides what to do next. A text-only response ends the turn.
      </p>

      <div class="loop-diagram" style="margin-top: 32px;">
        <div class="node">Prompt</div>
        <span class="arrow">→</span>
        <div class="node">LLM</div>
        <span class="arrow">→</span>
        <div class="node">Typed tools</div>
        <span class="arrow">→</span>
        <div class="node">Figma scene graph</div>
      </div>
      <p class="muted" style="margin-top: 16px; font-size: 14px;">
        Sessions reset only on "New Design". Conversation state is kept in one flat journal. If the current user turn crosses the model budget, large tool arguments from that turn may be compressed before the next model request; there is no separate cross-turn summary layer.
      </p>

      <h2 style="margin-top: 64px;">Choose the model path</h2>
      <p class="lead muted" style="margin-top: 16px;">
        The plugin and MCP surfaces do not configure models in the same place. In the plugin, you connect a provider and choose a model ID. On the MCP path, the STDIO client supplies its own model and calls Genable's tool surface.
      </p>

      <div class="models-table-wrap">
        <table class="models-table">
          <thead><tr><th>Surface</th><th>Connection</th><th>You configure</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Plugin</td><td>OpenAI-compatible</td><td>Endpoint, model ID, API key</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Plugin</td><td>Anthropic-compatible</td><td>Endpoint, model ID, API key</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Plugin</td><td>Gemini</td><td>Endpoint, model ID, API key</td></tr>
            <tr><td>MCP</td><td>STDIO client</td><td>Model in the client; Genable MCP server config</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h2 style="margin-top: 64px;">Detailed prompt patterns</h2>
      <p class="lead muted" style="margin-top: 16px;">
        A useful brief gives the model decisions to work from. Name the audience and visual direction, then add the Figma constraints that should survive into the file.
      </p>

      <div class="patterns">
        <div class="pat">
          <h3>Start with intent and hierarchy</h3>
          <p class="muted">Give the agent more than a page category. Identify who the design serves, what should lead, and the visual character to avoid a generic shell.</p>
          <blockquote>"Audience: operations leads comparing tools. Calm, editorial, high information clarity. One focal point; evidence before pricing."</blockquote>
        </div>

        <div class="pat">
          <h3>Specify the variant matrix up front</h3>
          <p class="muted">When related states matter, name the axes and values rather than leaving the model to infer them.</p>
          <blockquote>"Solid / outline / ghost × small / medium / large × default / hover / disabled. Expose Variant, Size, and State."</blockquote>
        </div>

        <div class="pat">
          <h3>Ask for the token model explicitly</h3>
          <p class="muted">If variables and modes matter to the handoff, say which semantics to create and which supported properties to bind.</p>
          <blockquote>"Brand collection with light and dark modes. Semantic text, surface, border, and accent colors. Bind fills, strokes, gaps, and padding where supported."</blockquote>
        </div>

        <div class="pat">
          <h3>Use measurable constraints where they help</h3>
          <p class="muted">Mood establishes direction; dimensions and scale steps make layout intent less ambiguous.</p>
          <blockquote>"Use the existing spacing variables. Keep the content column near 720px, use a compact card density, and reserve the largest type step for one headline."</blockquote>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2 style="margin-top: 64px;">Two surfaces, two model paths</h2>
      <p class="lead muted" style="margin-top: 16px;">
        In the plugin, provider configurations are stored through Figma <code>clientStorage</code>. Requests go to the endpoint you configure; some presets can use a relay when browser-network constraints require it. With <code>genable-mcp</code>, model access stays in your MCP client and the local server relays typed operations over WebSocket to the plugin running in Figma Desktop. Review the data and billing terms of the provider or client you choose.
      </p>

      <div style="margin-top: 64px; padding: 32px; border-radius: var(--r-lg); background: var(--bg-deep);">
        <strong style="font-size: 18px;">Want to follow the project or file a bug?</strong>
        <p class="muted" style="margin-top: 8px; margin-bottom: 16px;">
          The public project repository is MIT-licensed and includes the site, published assets, changelog, and issue tracker.
        </p>
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="https://github.com/musepy/genable" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">GitHub →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  h2 { font-size: 36px; }
  h3 { font-size: 22px; margin-bottom: 8px; }

  .loop-diagram {
    display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 12px;
    background: var(--bg-deep); padding: 24px; border-radius: var(--r-lg);
  }
  .node {
    padding: 12px 18px; border-radius: 10px; background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--hair); font-weight: 600; font-size: 15px;
  }
  .arrow { color: var(--muted); font-size: 18px; }

  .models-table-wrap { margin-top: 24px; overflow-x: auto; }
  .models-table { width: 100%; min-width: 620px; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 15px; }
  .models-table th, .models-table td { padding: 12px 16px; text-align: left; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hair-soft); }
  .models-table th { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.18em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--micro); font-weight: 700; }

  .patterns { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 32px; margin-top: 32px; }
  .pat { padding: 24px; border-left: 3px solid var(--accent); background: var(--surface); border-radius: 0 var(--r) var(--r) 0; }
  .pat blockquote {
    margin: 12px 0 0; padding: 14px 18px; border-radius: 10px;
    background: var(--bg-deep); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--ink-2); line-height: 1.55;
  }
</style>
